config THUMBLE_I2C_PROBE
    bool "Periodically log an I2C bus scan and the IQS5xx product number"
    depends on I2C && GPIO
    help
      Bring-up aid for the TPS65: every 10 s, scan the trackpad's I2C bus,
      log every address that ACKs, the RDY pin level, and the IQS5xx
      product/project/version registers read at 0x74. Only for the USB
      logging build.

config THUMBLE_IQS5XX_TUNE
    bool "Apply extra IQS5xx trackpad settings after the driver's init"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_AZOTEQ_IQS5XX_ENABLED && I2C
    help
      Sets the TPS65's active and idle-touch report rates, which the
      community driver leaves at the pad's 13 ms / 50 ms defaults.

if THUMBLE_IQS5XX_TUNE

config THUMBLE_IQS5XX_REPORT_RATE_MS
    int "Active and idle-touch report rate (ms)"
    default 10
    range 4 50
    help
      Lower is smoother but uses more power while a finger is on the pad.
      QMK uses 10 ms. Idle and low-power rates are left at the pad defaults.

endif
